/* ==== src/behaviors/b01_effects1a.js ==== */
/* Batch b01_effects1a: ports of battle_anim_effects_1.c (first half) sprite callbacks.
   Ordered by impact (number of moves using the callback). IsContest() is always FALSE, so only
   the battle branches are kept.

   RUNTIME REQUESTS:
   - copyPaletteColors(srcOffset, dstOffset, count): LoadPalette(&gPlttBufferUnfaded[src], dst, PLTT_SIZEOF(count))
     inside the palette buffer (AnimLockOnTarget_Step4 copies colours 8-9 of the lock-on palette onto
     colours 1-2: the reticle turns red). Recorded with the runtime's copyPalColors (pal[slot].copies =
     [[src, dst, n]]), the format the renderers' palette pipeline applies.
   - isBattlerSpriteVisible(b) differs from battle_anim.c: C returns TRUE when the battler is present and
     (!battlerData[b].invisible || !gSprites[b].invisible), i.e. a battler hidden by monbg (drawn on the BG)
     still counts as visible unless it is semi-invulnerable. The runtime returns
     present && (!sprite.invisible || semiInvisible), so Air Cutter (monbg ANIM_DEF_PARTNER) lost the
     between-both-targets position in doubles. Local faithful copy: IsBattlerSpriteVisible below. The same
     runtime helper feeds getAnimBattlerSpriteId / getBattlePalettesMask.
   - gAnimMoveIndex: read here as A.W.moveId (the move's id string, e.g. 'MOVE_CORE_ENFORCER'); a named
     accessor (A.gAnimMoveIndex) would be cleaner. */
