/* Battle FX Lab — HD layer, v3 move work, group D: rock and ground moves, hazards, rock / spike / crystal meshes, field and terrain effects
   Loaded after v3.js (configs and kits here override earlier files). See docs/V3_AUTHORING.md.
   Building blocks (all prefixed d_):
     meshes   d_shard (a jagged cut-stone blade), d_caltrop (a four-pointed spike), d_gem (a brilliant-cut gem)
     cells    d_crack (a dark broken-earth fissure with a lighter crumbled lip), d_hole (a dug pit), d_web (an irregular web
              for the ground), d_rune (an ancient glyph ring), d_furrow (tilled soil), d_arrow (an energy arrowhead)
     FX       d_debris (stone / soil / shell chunks on ballistic arcs: tumble, one bounce, a puff of dust where they land),
              d_crack (a crack that opens in the ground), d_quake (replaces the generic quake on ground moves: dark cracks
              spreading from the source, rolling dust, pebbles that jump), d_column (soil and rock erupting from the
              ground), d_sink (a battler lurches into the ground), d_hide (a battler hidden while the move hides it),
              d_aura (dragon energy wrapped round a battler), d_sweep (an energy arc swept through a target), d_funnel
              (a twisting funnel of streaks with debris), d_hazard (traps that stay on the foe's side: caltrops, toxic
              barbs, floating stones, a web)
     kits     d_rock (runtime rock sprites as tumbling cut-stone meshes with dust), d_bone (a swung / thrown ivory bone),
              d_shell (Shell Smash's halves: a shaded shell that cracks and bursts), d_blade (stone blades from the ground)
   As everywhere in the HD layer, effects key off the runtime's sprites, the plan's hits / births and the script's tasks;
   timing and outcomes are never changed. */
