/* ==== src/hd/v3_e.js ==== */
/* Battle FX Lab — HD layer, v3 move work, group E: status and support moves: psychic, sound, stat, item, protection, room, symbol moves
   Loaded after v3.js (configs and kits here override earlier files). See docs/V3_AUTHORING.md.
   Group E visual language (every name here carries the e_ prefix; nothing earlier is reassigned or wrapped):
     sound     e_sound    wavefront arcs from the mouth that travel to the target and make it shiver (Growl, Screech...)
     gaze      e_glint / e_gaze   a star glint in the user's eyes, a thin glare streak to the target, a shiver
     reaction  e_shiver / e_cue   the target shivers, cowers; small status cues (sleep Zs, dizzy stars, sparks...)
     shields   e_dome / e_wall    a glassy bubble round the user (Protect...), a slanted wall of light toward the foes
     healing   e_heal     a soft column of light, a glowing ground ring and rising motes: restorative, never a burst
     powders   e_powder   fine coloured powder drifting down onto the target
     field     e_sky / e_field / e_room / e_env   weather, terrains and rooms change the arena (within the theme caps)
     objects   e_orbit / e_toss / e_seal  lit objects circling the user, item pouches tossed, padlock seals
   All effects start on the move's own script events (a template, a task, a background command) or at fixed frames;
   timing, sprite paths and outcomes stay the runtime's. */
